            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0060" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.90H/67: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-13T17:00:00+03:25">March 13, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 13—1:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Supplementing my No. 64, March 12, I believe that if Department agrees to
                    name a Minister Plenipotentiary to Afghanistan it may be possible to obtain
                    consent of Afghan Government to Thayer’s proceeding to Kabul for purpose of
                    opening Legation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
